it's International Women's Day and we're  here to celebrate the cultural economic  and social achievements of women around  the world I've got one amazing woman  here with me this is Patricia bright she  is the new cover girl for Glamour and  we're here to talk about all things  International Women's Day I'm really  excited as well I love the idea of just  empowering and supporting women even  just by telling my own story tell me has  anybody really helped you on the ladder  to success today is there one woman that  particularly stands out who wasn't a  member of your family I would say I've  got loads of inspirations in this space  of the internet in YouTube and there's a  lady called Marie Forleo who's kind of  like a motivational speaker she has this  amazing course and I remember her just  sharing her story and just being really  inspired by her in this digital space as  a young black woman growing up in the UK  today did you feel the opportunities  were open to you or did you feel you  often faced brick walls and closures I  felt like things would be maybe a touch  harder for me because one woman too  black that not necessarily everyone  would know where I came from or  necessarily relate to me but you know I  was lucky enough to be part of two  things right when I got my first job the  way I ended up getting that job was by  attending something could the Women in  Technology dinner and I was also part of  a community called  SEO which was to get black people into  all the top investment banks at the top  law firms and all the top kind of  financial institutions so I had the  backing to get myself into those circles  so that whatever limitations there were  that I could at least try and be part of  a community who would support me through  them but the fact that I needed to be  part of things like that to get the  roles obviously shows that there were  some barriers but I was happy that there  are opportunities like that for me who  told you about these opportunities very  hard to know because growing up I didn't  know so I first worked in investment  banking before I started becoming a  youtuber and I studied accounting and I  met a  guy who was on a finance course and he  got a job a banking is like there's  really good opportunities check out the  website for one of the first films that  I worked for and there was an  opportunity to come for this Women in  Technology dinner what do you think the  biggest barrier is for young women today  who are trying to succeed in the  workplace I think one of the barriers is  sometimes not believing that you can  necessarily do it I think it's really  important for girls to know that you can  break through it and you can bring your  feminine energy to a space and actually  make it better do you think that maybe  when you say bring your feminist energy  do you think that women feel they can't  be themselves do you think they feel  that they need to be maybe or reserved  or more masculine in some way I do feel  like people feel like they have to go  one way or the other so I'm quite  dominant woman sometimes I'm like oh  maybe I should be a bit more girly and  then there are some who are a bit more  maybe reserved and they think maybe they  need to change themselves but I think  not every individual the best way to be  successful is to be your best version of  yourself  there isn't an issue with it you just  have to kind of own that and share it  with the teams or the people that you  work with that this is the way you are  and they can adapt themselves to work  with you can you think of a time that  you've made a crack in your glass  ceiling that you feel particularly proud  of I feel like I'm doing that now with  my own youtube channel and just kind of  create in my own space and my own  businesses and I've worked with  different management companies and  agencies in the past which often were  run by men but you know I decided to  kind of bring a lot of stuff in-house  and partner and employ more women and  more girls not for positive  discrimination but just because I  connect with them as one I feel like the  fact that I'm able to do that and be in  that position is breaking a glass  ceiling have you ever had a time where  you faced discrimination at work and how  did you deal with it I'm not sure if it  was that I felt that it was specifically  discrimination maybe feeling a little  bit left out as I keep mentioning I was  really an amalgam  environment and it's like don't really  know how to get involved you know you're  talking about the football or your  favorite beers and that kind of stuff  and I'm just like I like lipstick but  I'm not gonna have that conversation for  me overcoming it was kind of having to  just get involved like when they went  down to the pub I would join them at the  pub and have a bit can you think over  time as a woman that you've triumph over  tragedy  I wouldn't say triumph over tragedy I  just say try out you know childbirth  being a mum I feel like that to me is a  triumph and you know being self-employed  as well under mum and having to combine  the two how do you juggle it all how do  you make it all work it's not easy it is  quite hard to make it work I think  routine order and just you know being  that multitasking woman is the way to  make it work what does feminism mean to  you today for me personally feminism  means appreciating the difference  between men and women  I feel fundamentally we're very  different and the values that women have  are extremely extraordinary in my  opinion and it should be on the same  level and we should be treated in the  same way that men are even though we are  different what I hopes and dreams do you  have for women for your daughter in the  future I hope that women will feel  confident to embody themselves as they  are and that they don't have to change  or adapt or be more one way or more  another way to fit in or to get what  they actually deserve as a human being  in life so for more videos like this and  if you want to see what happened behind  the scenes of my color shoot make sure  you subscribe to the glamour UK YouTube  channel
 

